 to a redesigned front  reminiscent of the golf gti it's been  given the gti's 2-liter direct injection  turbocharged engine which pumps out 135  kilowatts the interiors pay homage to  the original shiroko with additional  instruments  bmw has broken new ground with its  2-series active tourer its first compact  mpv with front-wheel drive equally  unusual is the three-cylinder 100  kilowatt engine the seats are now 12  centimeters higher and the back seats  can be pushed forward 12 centimeters too  allowing additional luggage space in the  468 liter rear the active tourer starts  at 27 200 euros in germany  the astra is one of opel's most  important models whether as a three-door  gtc sports coupe or as a sports tour  station wagon now the company in  russeltheim germany has unveiled a new  range of engines for both the astra  family and for its other cars  jurgen keller says the gm subsidiary has  a new 1.6 liter gasoline engine and a  1.6 liter diesel and it's calling this  the whisper diesel it's extremely quiet  but has great performance and it offers  power even at lower rpms  we're testing this whisper diesel in the  beefier 100 kilowatt version found in  the astra sports tour automotive  journalist jens meinert is going to put  the new power plant through its paces  while listening closely  the new diesel is especially frugal opel  says it's the most fuel-efficient engine  in its range using 3.9 liters per 100  kilometers and in the smaller 81  kilowatt version it's even 3.7  jens says the engine really is very  quiet it's not only agile and relatively  sporty but also unusually smooth for a  diesel it's a very pleasant engine  one great detail is a sport button that  gives the astra more pep it changes its  steering and performance profile but  also switches the instrumentation to red  from cool white  vexit  both the practical sports tourer and the  sporty astra gtc feature this trick with  the display  now jens turns his attention to the 1.6  liter turbocharged gasoline engine  the gtc is designed for high performance  and that becomes clear in its handling  the gtc's technical data drive the point  home  the turbo engine's 1.6 liters generate  147 kilowatts accelerating it from zero  to 100 kilometers per hour in 7.9  seconds at 6.6 liters per hundred  kilometers fuel consumption is moderate  but only if it's driven gently  the motor  is the engine has been completely  redesigned with multiple markets in mind  gm plans to sell it in the us later it's  a great engine with almost effortless  power there's hardly a trace of turbo  lag in many turbocharged engine the  power kicks in only after a delay and  that's a big plus the engine also has a  beautiful sound it's relatively muted  but gets nice and throaty when you  really fire it up  so whether you choose the practical tour  with its easily folded down rear seats  or opt for the sporty gtc you can treat  yourself to one of the new engines we  tested  it's a common sight a truck traveling  along the highway  but the drivers not steering like in a  science fiction film  at daimler the future of trucking has  already begun this demonstration as part  of a technology event on an unopened  motorway section near monteborg has  caused a sensation in freight haulage  wolfgang bernhard head of daimler trucks  says the mercedes-benz future truck 2025  represents the company's vision for  transport and long distance services a  decade from now  for years daimler has been one of the  leading companies in active and passive  driving assistance systems for both cars  and trucks with safety systems including  proximity control assist stop and go  assist active brake assist 3 and lane  keeping assist these trucks already  offer a high level of safety but what is  now being demonstrated goes even further  says this is a world premiere a truck  that can drive autonomously that means  it can drive all by itself at 80  kilometers per hour without the driver  having to steer it can accelerate or  break stays right in the lane and is  very very safe  autonomous driving is made possible by  networking and augmenting existing  technology with cameras and radar  sensors when the message appears on the  display the driver can activate the  system and turn his seat 45 degrees away  from the steering wheel thanks to the  so-called highway pilot the truck can  now travel without driver input  this system can adjust to a wide variety  of driving situations for example if an  emergency vehicle approaches it can  automatically pull over to the right to  allow it to pass and then return to the  lane without driver intervention the  driver can still take over at any time  but how do truckers feel about that  hans luft is a truck driver  he says the new system is good and less  stressful once you get used to it  it takes some time to get used to  letting go of the steering wheel and  taking your eye off the road  by letting the truck take care of the  driving he says he has time to take care  of other activities in the  cabin foreign  cameras and radar sensors around the  vehicle enable drivers to pay attention  to other things but there's no word from  daimler as to what this technology will  cost autonomous driving is ready for use  in everyday trucking operations freight  haulers that watch the road promise to  make long distance transport safer  this extreme athlete and record breaker  is felix baumgartner of austria he began  his career in the mid-1990s as a base  jumper completing over 2600 jumps so far  you may remember him from 2012 when he  jumped from the edge of the stratosphere  now he's got a new challenge the 24  hours nurburgring race  the austrian former rally driver sepp  hider is leading the audi race  experience team he's only got a few  weeks to turn felix into a real racing  car driver as one of four drivers it's  key that he contribute to the team's  success  the team's leader says their goal is  clear he wants them to get into the top  ten he says they prepared felix well and  felix has also done as much as he can to  get himself in shape they have to do  what they can to minimize any mistakes  swiss racer rahel fry drives felix  around the grand prix track at the  nurburgring to find the ideal racing  line and the entry and breaking points  he's got to know the track like the back  of his hand  fry  goals are always extreme and he wants to  do it as fast as possible  that may be a good quality but for a  24-hour race you need patience she  points out that he breaks too late after  the cusp in the race you only have a  moment to get it right but she thinks  this is really a good start  on the track felix drives kilometer  after kilometer lap after lap always  pushing the car closer to its limits  he's got to make the 419 kilowatt audi  r8 lms ultra as tame and as safe as a  kitten now he's ready  this is not only felix's first try but  also the high point of his ambitious  from heaven to green hell project it  seems his dream has come true competing  on the north loop of the nurburgring  known as green hell and often considered  the world's most spectacular racing  track felix baumgardner and teammates  pierre koffer marco werner and frank  biela are competing against 30 other  teams in the gt3 class they're all going  for overall victory setting out after  the leader a mclaren  eight top makes line up at the start  including bmw mercedes and porsche and  audi is sending eight r8 lms ultras onto  the track at 4 pm the 165 competitors  start the 24 hour race on the 25  kilometer north loop stretch kevin estra  in the orange mclaren had the best start  but a bit further back the battle for  positions begins felix is the fourth  driver in the audi team which is  currently in eighth place he seems a  little surprised at how fast the  professional racers start their day  felix says you see the drivers are  prepared to take bigger risks in a  24-hour race and they go at it a bit  harder he adds it's obvious from the  beginning they give it their all  at 8 17 p.m the race has been going on  for over four hours and felix  baumgardner has to buckle in  he says they're only in ninth place and  he hopes the team won't lose too many  places because of him he admits he just  doesn't have the pacing and performance  skills of the best drivers but thinks he  can hold his own  felix's lap time is around 9 minutes  which is very respectable for a rookie  the top drivers are just about 30  seconds faster he doesn't take any  unnecessary risks and hands over the  unscathed car  felix baumgartner says he managed to get  through but it was pretty difficult  there are often three or four slower  cars ahead of you and each one swerves  in a different direction so the driver  has to maneuver around them what also  made things difficult was the low-lying  sun  felix is recovering from his first  performance and tries to get some sleep  but just after sunrise he's ready again  his second performance in the 24 hour  race is lined up  at six in the morning felix gets into  the car race for the second time at the  moment his team is in overall eighth  place his second performance is better  he seems more at ease with the  conditions and for the first time he  completes a lap in under 9 minutes at 8  minutes 59.7 seconds on the stopwatch  his best lap time on the north loop so  far  felix says he feels comfortable on  nearly every part of the track his  favorite is the north luke he even  prefers it to the grand prix stretch  felix's parents are there for his third  and last race keeping their fingers  crossed thanks to some good performances  from marco werner frank biele and pierre  cuffer and the newcomer felix  baumgartner the team managed to get into  the top ten  felix says everyone's more than happy  ninth place it couldn't get any better  in the first year  audi also secures an overall win at the  24-hour race 2014 with the r8 lms ultra  from team phoenix  and for felix one thing 