en he says they prepared felix well and  felix has also done as much as he can to  get himself in shape they have to do  what they can to minimize any mistakes  swiss racer rahel fry drives felix  around the grand prix track at the  nurburgring to find the ideal racing  line and the entry and breaking points  he's got to know the track like the back  of his hand  fry  goals are always extreme and he wants to  do it as fast as possible  that may be a good quality but for a  24-hour race you need patience she  points out that he breaks too late after  the cusp in the race you only have a  moment to get it right but she thinks  this is really a good start  on the track felix drives kilometer  after kilometer lap after lap always  pushing the car closer to its limits  he's got to make the 419 kilowatt audi  r8 lms ultra as tame and as safe as a  kitten now he's ready  this is not only felix's first try but  also the high point of his ambitious  from heaven to green hell project it  seems his dream has come true competing  on the north loop of the nurburgring  known as green hell and often considered  the world's most spectacular racing  track felix baumgardner and teammates  pierre koffer marco werner and frank  biela are competing against 30 other  teams in the gt3 class they're all going  for overall victory setting out after  the leader a mclaren  eight top makes line up at the start  including bmw mercedes and porsche and  audi is sending eight r8 lms ultras onto  the track at 4 pm the 165 competitors  start the 24 hour race on the 25  kilometer north loop stretch kevin estra  in the orange mclaren had the best start  but a bit further back the battle for  positions begins felix is the fourth  driver in the audi team which is  currently in eighth place he seems a  little surprised at how fast the  professional racers start their day  felix says you see the drivers are  prepared to take bigger risks in a  24-hour race and they go at it a bit  harder he adds it's obvious from the  beginning they give it their all  at 8 17 p.m the race has been going on  for over four hours and felix  baumgardner has to buckle in  he says they're only in ninth place and  he hopes the team won't lose too many  places because of him he admits he just  doesn't have the pacing and performance  skills of the best drivers but thinks he  can hold his own  felix's lap time is around 9 minutes  which is very respectable for a rookie  the top drivers are just about 30  seconds faster he doesn't take any  unnecessary risks and hands over the  unscathed car  felix baumgartner says he managed to get  through but it was pretty difficult  there are often three or four slower  cars ahead of you and each one swerves  in a different direction so the driver  has to maneuver around them what also  made things difficult was the low-lying  sun  felix is recovering from his first  performance and tries to get some sleep  but just after sunrise he's ready again  his second performance in the 24 hour  race is lined up  at six in the morning felix gets into  the car race for the second time at the  moment his team is in overall eighth  place his second performance is better  he seems more at ease with the  conditions and for the first time he  completes a lap in under 9 minutes at 8  minutes 59.7 seconds on the stopwatch  his best lap time on the north loop so  far  felix says he feels comfortable on  nearly every part of the track his  favorite is the north luke he even  prefers it to the grand prix stretch  felix's parents are there for his third  and last race keeping their fingers  crossed thanks to some good performances  from marco werner frank biele and pierre  cuffer and the newcomer felix  baumgartner the team managed to get into  the top ten  felix says everyone's more than happy  ninth place it couldn't get any better  in the first year  audi also secures an overall win at the  24-hour race 2014 with the r8 lms ultra  from team phoenix  and for felix one thing is clear  they'll definitely be back  you
 

